exports[`screen: 'help analyze' > en 40 plain 1`] = `
"  bladecp analyze <backup.tar.gz>
 ──────────────────────────────────────
  Reads a full cPanel backup on this
  computer and shows what it holds,
  what comes to BladeCP, what stays
  behind and the smallest plan it
  needs. Nothing is sent: the file
  never leaves this computer. With
  --prices it also asks BladeCP for the
  plans of your account, sending only
  the currency.

  Usage ────────────────────────────────
  bladecp analyze <backup.tar.gz>
      [--prices [--currency <code>] ]

  Arguments ───────────────────────────
  <backup.tar.gz>
    full backup made by cPanel
    (cpmove-user.tar.gz), up to 50 GB

  Options ─────────────────────────────
  --prices
    Also show the plans that fit and
    their prices now (needs sign-in)
  --currency <code>
    Show plans and prices in one
    currency (for example USD or BRL)

  The analysis runs here and reads the
  backup once, as a stream. Passwords,
  keys and the text of wp-config.php
  are never shown nor written to the
  report.

  Examples ────────────────────────────
  › bladecp analyze cpmove-site.tar.gz
    what migrates and the minimum plan,
    offline
  › bladecp analyze cpmove-site.tar.gz
    --prices
    the cheapest plan that fits, with
    the price of now
  › bladecp analyze cpmove-site.tar.gz
    --json
    the report for scripts (schema
    bladecp.analyze.v1)

  Exit codes ──────────────────────────
    0 the backup migrates (maybe with
      notes)
    2 the file is missing, empty or
      not a file
    6 the backup does not migrate as
      it is

  Global options ──────────────────────
  --json
    Print machine-readable JSON (no
    colors, no prompts)
  --api-url <url>
    API address (default
    https://api.bladecp.com)
  --lang <en|pt-BR|es>
    Language for messages
  --debug
    Describe each request on stderr
    (the key is never shown)
  --verbose
    Same as --debug
  -h, --help
    Show help
  -v, --version
    Show the version

  See also  bladecp migrate
  <backup.tar.gz>"
`;

