exports[`screen: 'help migrate' > en 120 plain 1`] = `
"  bladecp migrate <backup.tar.gz>
 ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Uploads a full cPanel backup and migrates the site to BladeCP. The wizard picks the destination,
  uploads the file in parts that can be resumed, follows every phase and stops when the preview is
  ready for your review.

  Usage ──────────────────────────────────────
  bladecp migrate <backup.tar.gz> [--plan <id> --location <id>] [--domain <host>] [--yes]
      [--no-wait]

  Arguments ──────────────────────────────────
  <backup.tar.gz>   full backup made by cPanel (cpmove-user.tar.gz), up to 50 GB

  Options ────────────────────────────────────
  --plan <id>       Destination plan ID (see "bladecp destinations list")
  --location <id>   Destination location ID (see "bladecp destinations list")
  --domain <host>   Domain the migrated site will use
  -y, --yes         Do not ask for confirmation; accept the domain found in the backup and, when it
                    is the only one, the destination
  --no-wait         Stop after the backup is received instead of following the migration

  How it works ───────────────────────────────
  ◆  checks the file
  │
  ◆  uploads it in parts that can be resumed
  │
  ◆  reads the backup and confirms the domain
  │
  ◆  prepares the server and imports
  │
  ◆  preview ready for your review
  │
  ◇  you approve; pointing the domain is optional

  Examples ───────────────────────────────────
  › bladecp migrate cpmove-site.tar.gz
    guided wizard
  › bladecp migrate cpmove-site.tar.gz --plan 12 --location 3
    destination given, no list
  › bladecp migrate cpmove-site.tar.gz --yes --no-wait --json
    CI: upload, do not wait, answer in JSON

  Exit codes ─────────────────────────────────
    0 preview ready or migration complete       10 needs you (for example, the domain)
    9 the migration failed or was cancelled    130 upload paused, the progress is saved

  Global options ─────────────────────────────
  --json                 Print machine-readable JSON (no colors, no prompts)
  --api-url <url>        API address (default https://api.bladecp.com)
  --lang <en|pt-BR|es>   Language for messages
  --debug                Describe each request on stderr (the key is never shown)
  --verbose              Same as --debug
  -h, --help             Show help
  -v, --version          Show the version

  See also  bladecp analyze <backup.tar.gz> · bladecp destinations · bladecp migrations status <uuid> --watch"
`;

